	"narrative": {
		"northStar": "The Marked-Up Proof",
		"overview": "A printed page somebody has gone over with a pen and a yellow highlighter. The paper is plain (white in light mode, a blue-black in dark), the text is a book serif, and everything mechanical (navigation, controls, subheads, figures, code) is set in a typewriter mono, as if annotated in the margin. The yellow does one job: it marks what matters, from \"Lazy\" in the hero to the page you are on in the sidebar to the matched letters in a search result.\n\nDensity is that of a reference book rather than a marketing page: one column of measured prose, tables that size to their numbers, controls drawn as thin ruled outlines. Surfaces are flat; separation comes from hairlines and a slightly lifted alternate paper, never from cards or shadows. Charts are allowed exactly two hues, Ekrina blue and the compared library's orange, so that every chart reads as a duel rather than a rainbow.",
		"keyCharacteristics": [
			"Serif for reading, mono for everything you operate or measure.",
			"One highlighter yellow, always a background with dark ink on it.",
			"Two chart hues, one per side of the comparison.",
			"Flat paper and hairline rules; no elevation at rest.",
			"Dark is the default theme; light overrides it token by token."
		],
